WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.188
Each test ends in one of six
statuses, from the tool's own source.

2
00:00:04.188 --> 00:00:06.588
Passed: the configuration matched.

3
00:00:06.588 --> 00:00:07.988
Failed: it didn't.

4
00:00:07.988 --> 00:00:12.649
Investigate: the tool needs a person
to look before it's a finding or not.

5
00:00:12.649 --> 00:00:17.690
Skipped: the test didn't run, and it
carries a reason, such as not licensed,

6
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.775
not connected, not applicable,
not supported, or timed out.

7
00:00:21.775 --> 00:00:25.213
Planned: the test is still
under construction in the tool.

8
00:00:25.213 --> 00:00:27.987
And error: the test couldn't be evaluated.

9
00:00:27.987 --> 00:00:31.900
A pillar owner reads their tab
with the risk and status filters,

10
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.263
and notes every investigate, skipped
and error result, with its reason.

11
00:00:36.263 --> 00:00:38.813
They also note every failed result whose

12
00:00:38.813 --> 00:00:41.438
feature may not exist
in the tenant's cloud.

13
00:00:41.438 --> 00:00:45.310
That last case matters for federal
tenants, and we'll come back to it.
